    "All enumerate Get-ADComputer -Filter * and loop through the resulting names, requesting immediate forced GP refresh and issuing remote Invoke-Command { gpupdate /force }.",
    "All request downloading PsExec using the undefined-in-file $PsExecUri. This does not establish a concrete network endpoint or successful download.",
    "The 7a224c31ac1a and 5d266a3c8e5b variants copy the executable through each target C$ share into Windows\\Temp. The e64e2819a8ee variant omits this copy and assumes the remote file already exists.",
    "Each variant invokes PsExec with -accepteula -d -s and a remote host, launching the remote Temp program with --password and --system. The extended XML also supplies --fast. These are program activation arguments, not evidence of credential theft.",
    "The script never assigns the GPO Id to $guid. Unless initialized by the calling session, the preferences directory has an empty GUID and does not address the newly created policy. Placeholder task name/date/GUID values are also left unchanged.",
